meta {
  name: Delete the account
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Apple-Authorization-Code: {{appleAuthCode}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Delete the account

  Permanently deletes the user and all their trips, then asks the identity provider to delete the sign-in account. Provider cleanup is best effort: a failure is logged and does not fail the request. Not undoable. An app that signed the user in with Apple must send `X-Apple-Authorization-Code`, obtained by asking Apple for a fresh authorization at deletion time (a code is single-use and expires after about 5 minutes); the server uses it to revoke the user's Sign in with Apple token, as Apple requires. Revoking is also best effort. Idempotent: repeating the call with a token that is still valid (for example after a lost answer) is again 204; there is no 404 here. Send the Apple code again on a retry, since the first one may have been used.
}
